From 8ae4f4582cb4a5cdb28c1504bd4bdc49ddc52b4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <phlink@local>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 21:46:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 9 plan 09-03 BundleReader codec + round-trip
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds chrome/browser/phlink/portability/bundle_reader.{h,cc} — the codec
half of the .phlinkbundle import pipeline:

- Verifies magic 'PHLB', format_version <= kSupportedMaxFormatVersion,
  KDF/AEAD ids, salt length, declared payload length.
- Derives the AEAD key with the bundle-specified Argon2id params (so a
  v1 reader does not need to know v2 defaults to import a v2 bundle that
  still uses Argon2id).
- AEAD-opens with the 69-byte header bound as AAD.
- zstd-decompresses, then walks the embedded ustar archive into
  manifest_ + entries_.
- Returns one of {kBadMagic, kUnsupportedVersion, kUnknownPrimitive,
  kBadPassphrase, kIntegrity, kTruncated, kIo, kOk}, mirroring
  docs/dev/profile-bundle-format.md §7.

Six unit tests cover the writer↔reader round-trip plus the five negative
paths (bad magic, truncation, wrong passphrase, unsupported version,
single-bit ciphertext tamper -> AEAD-tag rejection).

The import_service / Profile creation hookup / Import-card WebUI bits
enumerated in plan 09-03 are deferred to a follow-up sub-plan; this
patch lands the security-critical, format-validating piece in
isolation.
